00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.390
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and recently there
were loads of Cybermen filming at St Paul's

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.779
cathedral for the series 8 finale so in honor
of that I wanted to do a video for my Top

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:11.820
10 Cybermen episodes. Comic Con is next week
and even though Doctor Who isn't going I'm

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.660
still going to do a Doctor Who themed giveaway.
I'll explain that at the end of this video.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.400
Hello new people, if you're just finding me
for the first time I do Doctor Who videos

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.499
every week. Be sure to subscribe to get everything.
I've got a bunch of fun stuff planned for

00:00:22.499 --> 00:00:24.669
when the new episodes start.

00:00:24.669 --> 00:00:28.939
So just to explain the Cybermen at St Paul's
cathedral. The rumor is that the scene they

00:00:28.939 --> 00:00:33.790
were filming was an homage to a scene from
The Season 6 episode The Invasion. That's

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.020
Classic Who Season 6, it was a Second Doctor
episode.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:42.300
The episode is notable because it was the
last big Cybermen story until the 1975 episode

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.140
Revenge of The Cybermen. It featured the classic
Mondas design. I also think this was the first

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.850
television episode to feature St Paul's Cathedral
on screen. The only other reference I could

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:58.450
find to it being in an episode was in archival
footage during the series 5 finale The Big

00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.290
Bang.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:04.189
The scene itself looks like a big callback
plus there was a Mondas Cybermen head seen

00:01:04.189 --> 00:01:04.869
on set.

00:01:04.869 --> 00:01:08.670
I wonder if that means Steven Moffat is going
to retire the Cybermen for the remainder of

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:12.380
his tenure? Either way let's talk about the
Top 10 Cybermen episodes.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.630
Number 10 - Tomb of The Cybermen

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:18.229
This was their first appearance. The Second
Doctor arrives on the planet Telos with an

00:01:18.229 --> 00:01:22.679
archeological crew that tries to revive them.
The Doctor of course defeated them and resealed

00:01:22.679 --> 00:01:23.109
the tomb.

00:01:23.109 --> 00:01:28.999
It set up the whole idea of cybermats, the
little computer mice looking devices and the

00:01:28.999 --> 00:01:31.229
cyber controller, the one that controls all
cybermen.

00:01:31.229 --> 00:01:34.840
I have a feeling if this episode were made
today a cybermat would be seen zooming off

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.469
into the distance after the TARDIS left just
as a teaser that they would return at some

00:01:39.469 --> 00:01:42.630
point. You can thank Marvel Movie culture
for making those final credit scenes such

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:46.130
a huge deal today. Even though Soap Operas
on tv have been doing that kind of thing for

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:46.920
a long time.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:51.759
This episode was also notable because it's
the oldest surviving Second Doctor episode.

00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:58.259
Even though this original design looks a lot
different from the future Mondas cybermen,

00:01:58.259 --> 00:02:03.899
they are also consider Cybermen and part of
the Cyber Empire which included all pre-Cybus

00:02:03.899 --> 00:02:04.819
versions of the characters.

00:02:04.819 --> 00:02:08.709
I don't really consider the Cybus Industries
Cybermen as part of this group. But it gets

00:02:08.709 --> 00:02:13.530
a little confusing because during the 2005
reboot the 11th Doctor kept running into the

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.610
Cyber Legion Fleet in space. But they were
based on the Cybus designs. So their space

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.760
fleet should technically be different from
the Mondas Cyber Fleet.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.260
Number 9 - The Invasion

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:25.330
This was that last Cybermen episode before
the big break. It's them Invading current

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:29.340
day London and marching around in the streets
like awful space tourists before UNIT and

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:30.849
The Doctor took care of them.

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:34.819
There's a lot of interesting non-cybermen
stuff about this episode. From a production

00:02:34.819 --> 00:02:39.239
standpoint they were using the episode as
a test for the new format of the show. Instead

00:02:39.239 --> 00:02:43.930
of the way you see an hour long episode broken
into acts. The old Doctor who episodes were

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:49.390
physically separated into story arcs. It would
be like airing a Series 8 episode and cutting

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:52.709
it up into all the different acts and posting
those as separate episodes inside a single

00:02:52.709 --> 00:02:52.829
story.

00:02:52.829 --> 00:02:55.700
It's a little weird, but web series today
still do stuff like that.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:59.049
It was also intended as a sort of a follow
up to Web of Fear which was from season 5,

00:02:59.049 --> 00:03:02.079
the year before Invasion. That was another
Invasion modern day story that also involved

00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:04.140
UNIT and the Great Intelligence.

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:08.329
So be on the lookout for Great Intelligence
Easter Eggs in the Series 8 finale. That's

00:03:08.329 --> 00:03:12.709
not airing till November or December, they
haven't said if they'll be any off weeks in

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:18.769
series 8. It's totally possible they could
just air all 12 episodes back to back and

00:03:18.769 --> 00:03:21.299
then take a few weeks off before the christmas
special.

00:03:21.299 --> 00:03:23.329
Number 8 - The Five Doctors

00:03:23.329 --> 00:03:28.409
This is like porn for classic Cybermen fans.
It featured three different cyber controllers,

00:03:28.409 --> 00:03:31.989
even though two of them ate it pretty fast.
The episode itself is a little silly, but

00:03:31.989 --> 00:03:35.299
that was kind of the point. And art always
gets re-interpreted so people who watched

00:03:35.299 --> 00:03:37.939
this when it first aired probably feel different.

00:03:37.939 --> 00:03:40.719
It's so much fun though, the modern series
hasn't really shown off a lot of Gallifrey

00:03:40.719 --> 00:03:44.670
the way the classic series did. Although I
know a lot of you think that the TARDIS was

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:51.670
traveling into the Pocket Universe where Gallifrey
is hidden in the series 8 trailer.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:58.329
I'll totally save that for another video just
because we could spend all day talking about

00:03:58.329 --> 00:03:58.920
it.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:03.290
More Cybermen, moving on to Number 7 - Earthshock
This was another episode that brought them

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:08.180
back from a long hiatus. This aired during
1982 during the fifth Doctor's run. Before

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:13.109
this the last episode to feature them was
that 1975 episode Revenge of The Cybermen.

00:04:13.109 --> 00:04:18.000
The Doctor has to stop the Cybermen from crashing
a giant spaceship into the earth while the

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.180
powers of the world try to unite to fight
them off.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:24.460
There are a few more easter eggs relative
to Series 8 in here. For instance, Adric name

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:29.880
drops Romana and E-Space, which like the pocket
universe is extra dimensional.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:34.139
Capaldi's Into Darkness comment just makes
me feel like he will be traveling outside

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:38.190
normal space. But there are several places
that could take him. Especially if he's correcting

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.139
mistakes of the past.

00:04:39.139 --> 00:04:41.750
I'm not expecting Romana to come back or anything.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:44.069
Number 6 - Pandorica Opens

00:04:44.069 --> 00:04:48.199
This was legitimately a team up episode, so
I can't strictly call it a cybermen episode.

00:04:48.199 --> 00:04:51.569
But I just love the thought of that cyber
head chomping it's way after Amy and then

00:04:51.569 --> 00:04:55.729
Rory splitting it through the door. It's a
lot like the Daleks we saw in Asylum, even

00:04:55.729 --> 00:04:58.300
though they look terrible and ancient it doesn't
mean they're harmless.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:02.569
I always love team up episodes. Usually it's
the Doctor's friends coming to rescue him.

00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:05.380
But when all his enemies team up it's even
better.

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:07.280
Number 5 - Silver Nemesis

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:12.520
This is the kind of episode you'd get if you
combined Doctor Who with Merlin and Indiana

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:16.970
Jones. There are three different factions
trying to gain control of one of Rassilon's

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:19.699
artifacts that is used to defend Gallifrey
from attacks. The three factions being the

00:05:19.699 --> 00:05:22.280
Cybermen, A Sorceress and a group of Nazis.

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:27.080
This episode was from 1988 which falls between
Temple of Doom and Last Crusade and even if

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:30.970
the writers weren't overtly paying homage
to Indiana Jones, you have to admit that after

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:35.710
those movies anytime you think of Ancient
artifacts and Nazi collectors, you think of

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:36.729
that character.

00:05:36.729 --> 00:05:41.620
This was also the 25th Anniversary of Doctor
Who, just giving the Silver in the title a

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:45.599
nice double meaning. The producers tried to
get Prince Edward to appear in it, but the

00:05:45.599 --> 00:05:47.830
Royal Family declined.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:53.720
During the 50th Anniversary the Royal Family
did hold a party to celebrate the occasion.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:55.620
Number 4 - Nightmare In Silver

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:59.310
There are a lot of mixed feelings about this
episode. Neil Gaiman revealed that originally

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:04.080
it was written as a two part episode, so I
think any complaints about the story people

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:07.349
have were a result of mashing it all into
a single hour.

00:06:07.349 --> 00:06:11.639
I always wonder if those promo shots the used
like when it's revealed the Cybermen was the

00:06:11.639 --> 00:06:17.020
Turk are written in knowing they'll be used
as promos.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:22.210
And if you're not familiar, the Turk was a
so called automaton created in the late 18th

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:25.990
century. It was originally designed to be
the world's first robot that would play chess

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:28.650
against you, pretty well too.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:33.319
Secretly it was a puppet device operated by
a chess master hidden in the bowels of the

00:06:33.319 --> 00:06:33.729
machine.

00:06:33.729 --> 00:06:37.110
Which is why it was so funny when Warwick
Davis crawled out of the Cybermen Turk.

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:40.490
I also really liked the way they tried to
play with the idea of Mr Clever. The hybrid

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:45.030
organism created when the cyber planner merges
with the Doctor. It got a little silly, but

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:47.629
the gifs of Matt Smith were so hilarious.

00:06:47.629 --> 00:06:52.860
The real surprise there was that the Cybermen
found a way to thwart the Doctor's physiological

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:56.370
incompatibilities and assimilate him in mind
if not in body.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:58.289
Number 3 - Revenge of the Cybermen

00:06:58.289 --> 00:07:02.289
This was the first time they were brought
back after long hiatus. They hadn't gotten

00:07:02.289 --> 00:07:04.479
a big episode of their own for seven years
prior.

00:07:04.479 --> 00:07:08.919
The fourth Doctor learns about a plot where
the Cybermen are infecting people to eliminate

00:07:08.919 --> 00:07:14.050
the threat of Gold. One of the Mondas Cybermen
weaknesses was Gold, the metal affected their

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:15.990
organic breathing parts.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:20.430
This was also the story that aired directly
after Genesis of The Daleks and the episode

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:24.349
that aired right after it was Terror of The
Zygons, two other really important Fourth

00:07:24.349 --> 00:07:31.349
Doctor Stories.

00:07:31.419 --> 00:07:33.289
Number 2 - Army of Ghosts

00:07:33.289 --> 00:07:40.289
The Cybermen in this episode were like the
Hitchhiker's from hell. Just saying they had

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:45.810
nothing to do with the Void Ship Torchwood
was holding. They just used it as an dimensional

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:47.900
bus to jump into N Space.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:51.889
Unlike Pandorica Opens which came much later.
The Daleks and Cybermen fought against each

00:07:51.889 --> 00:07:54.870
other.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:58.400
These were the Cybus Versions that appeared
earlier during series 2. They were all sucked

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:05.400
into the void but they came back during The
Next Doctor Christmas Special with David Morrisey.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:12.759
Number 1 - Rise of the Cybermen/Age of Steel

00:08:12.759 --> 00:08:18.129
This was the introduction of the Cybermen
in the 2005 reboot with a brand new design.

00:08:18.129 --> 00:08:23.500
Like when Star Trek redesigned Klingons for
Next Generation. And as mid-season finale's

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:28.259
go, this was a hell of a two parter. In an
alternate universe, Cybus Industries and John

00:08:28.259 --> 00:08:32.710
Lumic created the cybermen as a way to cheat
death, he was terminally ill. And as expected,

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:34.659
the Cybermen went nuts.

00:08:34.659 --> 00:08:38.130
Supposedly in that universe about 5 Million
people on earth were assimilated. They broke

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:44.149
into N-Space a few times and iterations of
their design pop up every time we see cybermen.

00:08:44.149 --> 00:08:48.320
And just as an alt choice that wasn't a tv
episode a really awesome story is the Big

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:51.810
Finish audio drama Spare Parts. It's like
a Cybermen version of Genesis of The Daleks

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:54.480
starring Peter Davison.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:59.459
In that story, it's explained that the original
version of the Cybermen from Classic Who were

00:08:59.459 --> 00:09:03.360
from a race of people who lived on a planet
that was drifting too close to their sun and

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:06.940
as a measure of last resort they turned themselves
into cybermen.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:10.570
Gives new meaning to that phrase from the
Trailer, "Life Prevails".

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:14.230
But let me know what your favorite Cybermen
story is, it doesn't have to be an episode.

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:17.110
It can totally be a comic or one of the big
finish stories.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:21.760
Lots of Cybermen coming in Series 8, get excited.
We don't know what's going to bring them back

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:26.870
yet but I will be doing more weekly bonus
videos until episode 1 airs. That's going

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:30.160
to be on Saturday August 23rd. be sure to
subscribe to get everything.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:37.160
I'll leave the comic con giveaway open till
the week after.

